`data:` URLs put the full base64 payload inline in a `Uri` — semconv wants inline data as a `Blob`, and this can push multi-MB strings into a span attribute while `mime_type` stays `None` even though the data URL carries it.

#296 adds `image_from_url()` to `opentelemetry.util.genai.utils` which does exactly this split. Suggest waiting for #296 to merge and then reusing it instead of adding a second implementation here:

```python
if part_type == "image_url":
    ...
    return image_from_url(url, modality="image", capture_content=True)
```

@rads-1996 could you take a look at this one, given the overlap with #296?
